  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Vitalizing Unifying Neighboring Water management and Empowerment (VUNWE) Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The VUNWE integrated program will support two transboundary water course commissions, the Incomati and Maputo Water Courses Commission (INMACOM) and the Buzi, Pungwe and Save Water Courses Commission (BUPUSACOM). 
INMACOM is the water courses commission for the Incomati and Maputo River Basins, which are shared by South-Africa, Eswatini and Mozambique. Mbabane, the capital of Eswatini is hosting the commission. Through the PRIMA II project, EKN supported the establishment of INMACOM. 
BUPUSACOM is the water courses commission for the Buzi, Pungwe and Save River Basins, which are shared by Zimbabwe and Mozambique. In 2023, Zimbabwe and Mozambique signed the BUPUSA establishment agreement, the BUPUSA hosting agreement and the BUPUSA Data Sharing Protocol. The commission still has to be established.
The main aim for the proposed activity is:
- For INMACOM, to include the Umbeluzi River Basin in the Incomati and Maputo Water Courses Agreement and start implementing the five-year strategic plan and financial sustainability plan.
- For BUPUSACOM, to support the establishment of the BUPUSA commission and prepare bankable projects.
- For both, to strengthen the cooperation between the two commissions, in order to learn from each other&#x2019;s experiences (establishment of the commission, applying GEF funds, establishment of multi-stakeholder platforms and collaboration of INMACOM and BUPUSACOM with other SADC water courses commissions, especially ORASECOM).</narrative>
  </description>
